WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.525
Dashboard design should begin with the decisions users need to make.

00:00:03.525 --> 00:00:07.000
Before choosing charts or software, identify who will use the system,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
what questions they must answer, how quickly they need answers,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.000
and what action should follow.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
A home user may need to distinguish routine motion from a meaningful perimeter event.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.870
A small business may monitor access, camera availability, endpoint alerts,

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.000
and backup status.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.925
A laboratory or facility may care about restricted zones, environmental sensors,

00:00:23.925 --> 00:00:25.920
equipment health, and incident records.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.000
An enterprise team may need broader triage and ownership workflows.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Situational awareness answers what is happening now and what changed recently.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.995
Alert triage helps determine priority and ownership.

00:00:34.995 --> 00:00:38.000
Event review connects an alert to supporting evidence and prior activity.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Operational health shows whether the monitoring pipeline itself is functioning.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.950
Translate those goals into specific views.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:49.000
A triage view may emphasize new high-priority events, confidence, age, and assignment.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.000
An investigation view may show a timeline, related assets, logs, and clips.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.640
A health view may show failed collectors, storage pressure, delayed ingestion,

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.000
and notification errors.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Avoid a dashboard that displays data without supporting action.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.190
Large counters and colorful charts are not useful when a reviewer cannot tell what

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.000
requires attention,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.950
why it matters, or where to investigate next.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:11.000
Every prominent element should support a defined decision or workflow.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.950
Set success measures early.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.995
Useful measures include time to acknowledge important alerts,

00:01:15.995 --> 00:01:19.460
time to find supporting evidence, false-positive burden, unresolved event age,

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.000
ingestion delay, and service availability.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.190
These measures keep the dashboard focused on operational outcomes rather than visual

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.000
complexity.
